{"title":"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The average height of Ivan, Jackie and Ken is 4% larger than the average height of Ivan and Jackie. If Ivan and Jackie are each 175 cm tall, how tall is Ken?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since Ivan and Jackie are the same height, their average height must be the same as the height of one of them. Thus, their average height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa2c5db610c6d7c961d76200b986305e4f13db0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$175$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> cm.\n</p><p>Next, since the average height of all three of them is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b7a4fd8e4e9383a82f096e47fa5fde6ae1009c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" /> larger than the average height of just Ivan and Jackie, the average height of all of them must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba5f54eff96c8c2a2f1d8c2ed8158fc94adcdfab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$175 + 175 \\times 4\\% = 175 + 175 \\times \\frac{1}{25} = 175 + 7 = 182$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"405\" height=\"38\" /> cm\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be Ken's height. Since the average height of all three of them is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea9119513dcfff6adda7e89a8f0aa460eaed0305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$182$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> cm, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/0/5707e8287898673e8c1aacbf65ceb99bbae5f8a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{175 + 175 + k}{3} = 182$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"166\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a50ae70bf98df60f806a1816d467ab710150af1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k + 350}{3} = 182$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb50e4672a2c8f435472ee4f44c9ad3a8c18a4fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 350 = 182 \\times 3 = 546$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"196\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06625d954b9247ec430eef4504599fd3559fd40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 546 - 350 = \\boxed{196}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"176\" height=\"25\" /> cm\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC\">2017 CEMC CTMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Individual Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_4\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 4\">Individual Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_1\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 1\">Individual 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Individual 2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Individual 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_4\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 4\">Individual 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Individual 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Individual 6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 7 (page does not exist)